onal","affiliation":[{"name":"Nanjing University of Posts and Telecommunications,Department of Communication Engineering,Nanjing,China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Ting","family":"Wan","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Nanjing University of Posts and Telecommunications,Department of Communication Engineering,Nanjing,China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.23919\/aces-china66523.2025.11333113","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025,8,8]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,8,8]]},"container-title":["2025 International Applied Computational Electromagnetics Society Symposium (ACES-China)"]},{"DOI":"10.1002\/9781394474516.ch3","title":["Packaged Asynchronous Dynamic Random\u2010Access Memory"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/9781394474516.ch3","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,27]]},"published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,7]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,7]]},"container-title":["Computer Memories 3"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/iseae64934.2025.11041779","title":["Design of a 100G Ethernet Media Access Control Controller Based on Direct Memory Access"],"author":[{"given":"Haoqi","family":"Hao","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Group Corporation,The 32nd Research Institute of China Electronics Technology,Shanghai,China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Minhua","family":"Ren","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Group Corporation,The 32nd Research Institute of China Electronics Technology,Shanghai,China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/iseae64934.2025.11041779","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025,4,18]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,4,18]]},"container-title":["2025 7th International Conference on Information Science, Electrical and Automation Engineering (ISEAE)"]},{"DOI":"10.3390\/electronics12081792","title":["A Multi-User Collaborative Access Control Scheme Based on New Hash Chain"],"author":[{"given":"Zetian","family":"Wang","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Key Laboratory of Complex Systems Modeling and Simulation, HDU-ITMO Joint Institute, Hangzhou Dianzi University, Hangzhou 310018, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-6889-8481","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Yunfa","family":"Li","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Key Laboratory of Complex Systems Modeling and Simulation, School of Computer Science and Technology, Hangzhou Dianzi University, Hangzhou 310018, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Guanxu","family":"Liu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Key Laboratory of Complex Systems Modeling and Simulation, School of Computer Science and Technology, Hangzhou Dianzi University, Hangzhou 310018, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Di","family":"Zhang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Key Laboratory of Complex Systems Modeling and Simulation, School of Computer Science and Technology, Hangzhou Dianzi University, Hangzhou 310018, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.3390\/electronics12081792","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2023,4,10]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,4,10]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>As the threats to the Internet of Things (IoT) continue to increase, access control is widely used in various IoT information systems. However, due to the shortcomings of IoT devices such as low computing power, it is impossible to use high-performance methods to control user access. Although the emergence of the blockchain provides another way of thinking for access control, the implementation based on the blockchain requires the device to complete the proof of work (PoW) and requires the device to have high computing power. At the same time, most access control schemes existing today are intended for users to use alone, which cannot be applied to the field of multi-user coordinated access. Therefore, this paper proposes a multi-user collaborative access control scheme based on a new hash chain, which uses the identity information of multiple users as the seed value to construct the hash chain, and uses the hash chain as the PoW of the blockchain. An efficiency analysis showed that this method requires only a small amount of hash value calculation and can be applied to IoT systems with low computing power. The security analysis shows that the scheme can resist a variety of attack methods and has high security.<\/jats:p>","container-title":["Electronics"]},{"DOI":"10.56726\/irjmets89618","title":["A Comprehensive Review of Real-Time Collaborative Coding Platforms with Role-Based Access Control"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.56726\/irjmets89618","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,2,11]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,2,11]]},"container-title":["International Research Journal of Modernization in Engineering Technology &amp; Science"]},{"DOI":"10.1002\/9781394446629.ch6","title":["Asynchronous Static Random\u2010Access Memory as a Component"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/9781394446629.ch6","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,26]]},"published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,3]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,3]]},"container-title":["Computer Memories 2"]},{"DOI":"10.1002\/9781394446629.ch2","title":["Other Characteristics of a Semiconductor Random\u2010Access Memory"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/9781394446629.ch2","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,26]]},"published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,3]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,3]]},"container-title":["Computer Memories 2"]},{"DOI":"10.1002\/9781394446629.ch1","title":["Timing Characterization of a Semiconductor Random\u2010Access Memory"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/9781394446629.ch1","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,26]]},"published-online":{"date-p