"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-6547-9225","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Suwoong","family":"Lee","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Korea Institute of Industrial Technology, Daegu, Republic of Korea"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-2798-7154","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Byeong","family":"Hak Kim","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Korea Institute of Industrial Technology, Daegu, Republic of Korea"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2025.3586121","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2024.3432175","title":["Ethernet Packet-to-RS485 Data Transfer Bridge Application-Specific Integrated Circuit Incorporating Transmission Control Protocol and Static Random-Access Memory"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-2442-2983","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Guo-Ming","family":"Sung","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Electrical Engineering, National Taipei University of Technology, Taipei, Taiwan"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-8072-4759","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Chun-Ting","family":"Lee","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Electrical Engineering, National Taipei University of Technology, Taipei, Taiwan"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Zhi-Lun","family":"You","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Electrical Engineering, National Taipei University of Technology, Taipei, Taiwan"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Chih-Ping","family":"Yu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Electrical Engineering, National Taipei University of Technology, Taipei, Taiwan"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2024.3432175","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2024.3359250","title":["<i>H<sub>\u221e<\/sub>\n                  <\/i> Synchronization for Chaotic Lur\u2019e System With Uncertainty Based on Memory-Based Sampled-Data Control"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0003-3853-6986","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Wenbo","family":"Zhao","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"International School, Beijing University of Posts and Telecommunications, Beijing, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Wei","family":"Feng","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Artificial Intelligence, Tangshan University, Tangshan, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-8157-7519","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Chao","family":"Ge","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Artificial Intelligence, Tangshan University, Tangshan, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2024.3359250","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1103\/bmsv-mlq5","title":["Optimal Control of Bit Erasure in Stochastic Random Access Memory"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-8046-4056","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Songela W.","family":"Chen","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"id":[{"id":"https:\/\/ror.org\/01an7q238","id-type":"ROR","asserted-by":"publisher"}],"name":"University of California, Berkeley"},{"id":[{"id":"https:\/\/ror.org\/02jbv0t02","id-type":"ROR","asserted-by":"publisher"}],"name":"Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-2766-0688","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"David T.","family":"Limmer","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"id":[{"id":"https:\/\/ror.org\/01an7q238","id-type":"ROR","asserted-by":"publisher"}],"name":"University of California, Berkeley"},{"id":[{"id":"https:\/\/ror.org\/02jbv0t02","id-type":"ROR","asserted-by":"publisher"}],"name":"Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory"},{"id":[{"id":"https:\/\/ror.org\/02jbv0t02","id-type":"ROR","asserted-by":"publisher"}],"name":"Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory"},{"id":[{"id":"https:\/\/ror.org\/03c0kvc14","id-type":"ROR","asserted-by":"publisher"}],"name":"Kavli Energy NanoScience Institute"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1103\/bmsv-mlq5","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,6,16]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,6,16]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Energy costs of information processing are growing exponentially. Bit erasure is a key problem in this energy-information nexus, and a number of seminal relationships have been deduced regarding the relationship between thermodynamic costs and memory storage. To continue making progress in the modern era, however, requires confronting thermodynamic costs in realistic physical systems, which operate away from equilibrium. Here, we explore the thermodynamic costs of bit erasure in a complementary metal-oxide-semiconductor model of two types of random-access memory. We find dynamic random-access memory dissipates the least amount of energy when operated in the quasistatic limit, where errors are also minimized. By contrast, static random-access memory is most efficiently operated in finite time due to the energy required to maintain the state of the bit. We demonstrate a numerically robust optimization scheme using mean field theory and automatic differentiation, finding optimal protocols compatible with electrical engineering insights. These results provide a framework for operating realistic circuits in thermodynamically advantageous ways.<\/jats:p>","container-title":["PRX Energy"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/mlise70044.2026.11607496","title":["Failure-Gated Hierarchical Memory: Preventing Memory Pollution in Long-Horizon LLM Agents via Critic-Guided Write Control"],"author":[{"given":"Qizhi","family":"Liu","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"National Science Library","place":["Beijing, China"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Meng","family":"Wang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"National Science Library","place":["Beijing, China"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Jing","family":"Xie","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"National Science Library","place":["Beijing, China"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/mlise70044.2026.11607496","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026,5]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,5]]},"container-title":["2026 6th International Conference on Machine Learning and Intelligent Systems Engineering (MLISE)"]},{"DOI":"10.1002\/9781394446629.ch5","title":["Internal Organization of a Generic Asynchronous Static Random\u2010Access Memory"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/9781394446629.ch5","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,26]]},"published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,3]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,3]]},"container-title":["Computer Memories 2"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2025.3614728","title":["Speed Estimation in Induction Motor Drive Using Long Short-Term Memory-Sensorless Model Reference Adaptive System (LSTM-SMRAS) Control"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0001-8823-5298","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Gopal Lal","family":"Jat","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Electrical Engineering, Punjab Engineering College (Deemed to be University), Chandigarh, India"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-9505-4578","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Jagdish","family":"Kumar","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Electrical Engineering, Punjab Engineering College (Deemed to be University), Chandigarh, India"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Shiv","family":"Narayan","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Electrical Engineering, Punjab Engineering College (Deemed to be University), Chandigarh, India"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2025.3614728","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1155\/2023\/9842134","title":["Retracted: Blockchain-Based Privacy Access Control Mechanism and Collaborative Analysis for Medical Images"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1155\/2023\/9842134","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,10,11]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,10,11]]},"container-title":["Security and Communication Networks"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2025.3588035","title":["An Improved Rule-Based Energy Management System: Effective Solution to Achieve Collaborative Control of Batteries in Multi-Prosumers Community Microgrid"],"author":[{"given":"Jiawei","family":"Huang","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"State Key Laboratory of Advanced Electromagnetic Technology, School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering, Huazhong University of Science and Technology, Wuhan, China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-3954-6900","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Chengxiong","family":"Mao","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"State Key Laboratory of Advanced Electromagnetic Technology, School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering, Huazhong University of Science and Technology, Wuhan, China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"OR