tute, *Memory Div., Kioxia Corporation,Japan"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Kazuma","family":"Hasegawa","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Frontier Technology R&#x0026;D Institute, *Memory Div., Kioxia Corporation,Japan"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Xu","family":"Li","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Frontier Technology R&#x0026;D Institute, *Memory Div., Kioxia Corporation,Japan"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Yuichi","family":"Sano","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Frontier Technology R&#x0026;D Institute, *Memory Div., Kioxia Corporation,Japan"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Tomoya","family":"Sanuki","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Frontier Technology R&#x0026;D Institute, *Memory Div., Kioxia Corporation,Japan"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/imw68301.2026.11532787","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,10]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,10]]},"container-title":["2026 IEEE International Memory Workshop (IMW)"]},{"DOI":"10.4324\/9781003539148-4","title":["Challenges of collaborative working"],"author":[{"given":"Tara","family":"Webster-Deakin","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.4324\/9781003539148-4","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026,1,22]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,1,22]]},"container-title":["Collaborative Approaches to Widening Participation"]},{"DOI":"10.52202\/081497-0071","title":["The Research on Multi-Chain Collaborative Access Control for Industrial Internet of Things Systems"],"author":[{"given":"Jian","family":"WANG","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Hao","family":"XU","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Xingzhao","family":"CAO","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Wenjing","family":"GAO","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.52202\/081497-0071","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"container-title":["13th International Symposium on Project Management (ISPM2025)"]},{"DOI":"10.1016\/j.ipm.2024.103960","title":["Blockchain empowered dynamic access control for secure data sharing in collaborative emergency management"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-0371-3746","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Qi","family":"Wang","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-1399-7420","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Yi","family":"Liu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1016\/j.ipm.2024.103960","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025,5]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,5]]},"container-title":["Information Processing &amp; Management"]},{"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025,7,1]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>This study addresses limitations in single-alkali research by investigating mineral dissolution-precipitation dynamics and functional group transformations under multi-alkali conditions. Comparative experiments with concentration gradients were conducted to analyze chemical structure evolution and methane adsorption performance in alkalized anthracite. Brunauer\u2013Emmett\u2013Teller, scanning electron microscopy, x-ray diffraction (XRD), and Fourier-transform infrared spectroscopy (FTIR) analyses revealed alkaline solutions' synergistic regulation of hierarchical pore structures. Results show 1\u2009mol\/l potassium hydroxide (KOH) increased average pore diameter by 32% while reducing specific surface area by 24.6%, shifting pore dominance from microporous to macroporous structures with H3 hysteresis loops. High-concentration sodium hydroxide (NaOH) elevated surface fractal dimension (D1\u2009=\u20092.53) and enhanced pore connectivity by 3.2-fold. XRD\/FTIR characterization indicated KOH is superior mineral dissolution capacity, reducing aromatic lamellae stacking height by 37.8% and increasing alkyl chain (\u2013CH) content while decreasing reactive adsorption sites (\u2013CH2\/\u2013CH3). Alkaline conditions (pH\u2009&amp;gt;\u200912) promoted OH\u2212 driven aluminosilicate dissolution to alleviate pore blockage, alongside catalytic dissociation of carboxyl\/phenolic hydroxyl groups facilitating aromatic layer disassembly. This mineral-organic synergy generated interconnected nano-micro fracture networks, supporting methane desorption-seepage channel enhancement through structural reconstruction. The findings demonstrate coupled effects of mineral dissolution and organic matrix transformation in optimizing coalbed methane recovery efficiency with solution parameters quantitatively correlating to adsorption-seepage behavior modifications.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1063\/5.0273307","title":["Multi-scale collaborative control mechanisms of coal pores via alkalizing agents"],"author":[{"given":"Peng","family":"Wei","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-7293-1072","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Shanyang","family":"Wei","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Xingjie","family":"Wu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Hao","family":"Wang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Yitong","family":"Feng","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Huabang","family":"Wu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"published-online":{"date-parts":[[2025,7,1]]},"container-title":["Physics of Fluids"],"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,7,1]]},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1063\/5.0273307"},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2026.3668011","title":["A Collaborative Matching Control Method for the Electro-Hydraulic Hybrid Drive Swing System of Excavators Considering Energy Efficiency"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0001-7811-8901","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Jie","family":"Cheng","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Key Laboratory of Advanced Transducers and Intelligent Control System of Ministry of Education and Shanxi Province, Taiyuan University of Technology, Taiyuan, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Huijie","family":"Wang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Key Laboratory of Advanced Transducers and Intelligent Control System of Ministry of Education and Shanxi Province, Taiyuan University of Technology, Taiyuan, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-8042-2155","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Jiahai","family":"Huang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"College of Mechanical Engineering, Anhui University of Science and Technology, Huainan, Anhui, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-8148-1771","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Long","family":"Quan","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Key Laboratory of Advanced Transducers and Intelligent Control System of Ministry of Education and Shanxi Province, Taiyuan University of Technology, Taiyuan, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Lianpeng","family":"Xia","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Key Laboratory of Advanced Transducers and Intelligent Control System of Ministry of Education and Shanxi Province, Taiyuan University of Technology, Taiyuan, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Weinan","family":"Huang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Key Laboratory of Advanced Transducers and Intelligent Control System of Ministry of Education and Shanxi Province, Taiyuan University of Technology, Taiyuan, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-3013-9981","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Huimin","family":"Hao","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Key Laboratory of Advanced Transducers and Intelligent Control System of Ministry of Education and Shanxi Province, Taiyuan University of Technology, Taiyuan, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Xiaoyan","family":"Xiong","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Key Laboratory of Advanced Transducers and Intelligent Control System of Ministry of Education and Shanxi Province, Taiyuan University of Technology, Taiyuan, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2026.3668011","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.2139\/ssrn.7143461","title":["Failure Memory in Grid-World Agents"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0006-2038-3274","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Ishaan","family":"Verma","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.2139\/ssrn.7143461","issued":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>An agent that acts over many steps can waste effort by attempting the same blocked move more than once. This study measures whether persistent within-run memory of blocked state-action pairs reduces that waste in a simple grid world, and whether the reduction changes task outcomes. Two agents share an identical deterministic policy that ranks moves by Manhattan-distance reduction and breaks ties with a seeded action permutation. They differ in one respect. The baseline agent excludes a blocked pair for the next decision only, which gives immediate reactive recovery. The memory agent excludes a blocked pair for the rest of the run. The comparison uses 10 fixed mazes and 5 seeds, giving 100 paired runs. Persistent memory removed repeated blocked actions, reducing the mean from 35.12 to 0.00 per run, and cut mean blocked actions from 37.00 to 2.04. Success rate and mean total steps did not change: both agents reached the goal in 56 percent of runs and used 65.5 steps on average. The two agents behaved identically on the five mazes that both solve. They differed only on the five mazes where the baseline became trapped. On those mazes both agents still failed, because the greedy policy fell into oscillations between valid, unblocked cells, which blocked-action memory cannot detect. Persistent failure memory therefore reduced one class of repeated error without improving overall navigation. All code, data, and figures are released, and the full run reproduces to an identical fingerprint.<\/jats:p>"},{"DOI":"10.4324\/9781003539148-3","title":["Collaborative approaches towards widening participation"],"author":[{"given":"Tara","family":"Webster-Deakin","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.4324\/9781003539148-3","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026,1,22]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,1,22]]},"container-title":["Collaborative Approaches to Widening Participation"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/jiot.2025.3583009","title":["Efficient Collaborative Access Control Encryption Scheme for Cloud Storage"],"author":[{"given":"Ran","family":"Lingqin","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"State Key Laboratory of Public Big Data, Big Data Industry Application Research Institute, Guizhou University, Guiyang, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0009-1410-0612","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Peng","family":"Changgen","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"State Key Laboratory of Public Big Data, Big Data Industry Application Research Institute, Guizhou University, Guiyang, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Tan","family":"Weijie","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"State Key Laboratory of Public Big Data, Big Data Industry Application Research Institute, Guizhou University, Guiyang, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/jiot.2025.3583009","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025,9,1]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,9,1]]},"container-title":["IEEE Internet of Things Journal"]},{"DOI":"10.4337\/9781800372535.00015","title":["Agents of memory politics"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-7879-0725","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Laure","family":"Neumayer","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.4337\/9781800372535.00015","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,4,25]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,4,25]]},"container-title":["Handbook on the Politics of Memory"]},{"DOI":"10.36227\/techrxiv.176523350.08289935\/v1","title":["Memory Fabric for Conversational AI Agents: Enabling Shared and Persistent Memory Across Users"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0000-4183-4480","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Anjikya","family":"Tiwari","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"CoreAI, Microsoft Corp"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Vibhuti","family":"Gupta","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Biostatistics and Data Science, Medical Branch, University of Texas"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.36227\/techrxiv.176523350.08289935\/v1","issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,12,8]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Conversational AI is now the most widely adopted platform for interfacing with LLMs. Alongside LLMs these AI systems rely on contexts derived from past conversations and preferences to provide accurate and the most relevant responses to users. The knowledge base and past experiences contribute to long-term memory, while processing ongoing conversations generates short-term memory. Both long-term and short-term memories together provide a comprehensive and coherent context to the user. While most architectures focus on a single user context, there is an emerging need in conversational AI to provide a system to generate context from multiple individuals and\/or agents. Building on this foundation, we introduce memory fabric, a framework that allows conversational AI to leverage context drawn from multiple users to generate coherent responses in a multiuser setting. This review is a synthesis of foundational memory architectures, from early models such as Neural Turing Machines and Key-Value Memory Networks to recent systems like AutoGen, SRMT, AgentVerse, and SAMEP evaluated through the lens of memory fabric. It also addresses work on dialogue and agent memory, multi-agent shared-memory designs, privacy and provenance strategies, benchmarking standards, and system-level considerations. A systematic review of English articles using IEEE Xplore, ACM, arXiv, SpringerLink, and ACL anthology databases was performed. Only full-text studies reported between 2014 and 2025 were included for analysis. Following PRISMA guidelines, a total of 662 studies were identified, of which 27 studies met the inclusion criteria. Overall, this review presents a detailed analysis on leveraging contexts from multiple users in a shared environment in foundational memory architectures, offering an in-depth analysis of their strengths and shortcomings, along with recommendations and future research directions.<\/jats:p>"},{"DOI":"10.63282\/3050-9262.ijaidsml-v5i4p104","title":["Collaborative Shield: Strengthening Access Control with Federated Learning in Cybersecurity"],"author":[{"given":"Govindarajan","family":"Lakshmikanthan","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Sreejith Sreekandan","family":"Nair","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.63282\/3050-9262.ijaidsml-v5i4p104","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"container-title":["International Journal of Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, and Machine Learning"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/isset66828.2025.11185002","title":["Federated Learning-Enabled Collaborative Access Control for Medical Data with Multiple Authorities"],"author":[{"given":"Yifei","family":"Li","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"ZTE Corporation,Xi&#x2019;an,China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Zhichao","family":"Yuan","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Luohe Medical College,Luohe,China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Wei","family":"Liu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Xian University of Posts and Telecommunications,School of Cyberspace Security,Xi&#x2019;an,China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Hongyan","family":"Di","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Xian University of Posts and Telecommunications,School of Cyberspace Security,Xi&#x2019;an,China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/isset66828.2025.11185002","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025,7,24]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,7,24]]},"container-title":["2025 4th International Symposium on Semiconductor and Electronic Technology (ISSET)"]},{"DOI":"10.1145\/3719027.3744849","title":["<scp>BASTAG:<\/scp>\n                    Byte-level Access Control on Shared Memory using ARM Memory Tagging Extension"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-1539-229X","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Junseung","family":"You","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of ECE &amp; ISRC, Seoul National University, Seoul, Republic of Korea"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-1848-750X","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Jiwon","family":"Seo","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Cybersecurity, Dankook University, Yongin, Republic of Korea"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-6716-2915","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Kyeongryong","family":"Lee","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of ECE &amp; ISRC, Seoul National University, Seoul, Republic of Korea"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-7842-1719","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Yeongpil","family":"Cho","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Computer Science, Hanyang University, Seoul, Republic of Korea"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-6412-2926","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Yunheung","family":"Paek","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of ECE &amp; ISRC, Seoul National University, Seoul, Republic of Korea and Core Trust Link, Seoul, Republic of Korea"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1145\/3719027.3744849","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,19]]},"published-online":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,22]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,19]]},"container-title":["Proceedings of the 2025 ACM SIGSAC Conference on Computer and Communications Security"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/ricai68060.2025.11385199","title":["Modeling Method for Multi-Industrial Agents Collaborative Network in Complex Product Manufacturing"],"author":[{"given":"Yifan","family":"Pang","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Northwestern Polytechnical University, School of Mechanical Engineering,Xi&#x0027;an,China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Hao","family":"Bai","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Northwestern Polytechnical University, School of Mechanical Engineering,Xi&#x0027;an,China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Qiwei","family":"Xu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Northwestern Polytechnical University, School of Mechanical Engineering,Xi&#x0027;an,China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Yuanhao","family":"Li","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Northwestern Polytechnical University, School of Mechanical Engineering,Xi&#x0027;an,China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/ricai68060.2025.11385199","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,14]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,14]]},"container-title":["2025 7th International Conference on Robotics, Intelligent Control and Artificial Intelligence (RICAI)"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2024.3494818","title":["Finite-Time Guaranteed-Cost H<sub>\u221e<\/sub> Control of Time-Varying Systems With Actuator Saturation Based on Memory Dynamic Event-Triggered Mechanism"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-4349-5096","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Menghua","family":"Chen","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Electrical Engineering, Dalian Jiaotong University, Dalian, Liaoning, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Shuting","family":"Wang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Electrical Engineering, Dalian Jiaotong University, Dalian, Liaoning, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0003-8761-9761","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Xinping","family":"Wang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Electrical Engineering, Dalian Jiaotong University, Dalian, Liaoning, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-1289-047X","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Yunming","family":"Wang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Electrical Engineering, Dalian Jiaotong University, Dalian, Liaoning, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2024.3494818","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.7554\/elife.85694.sa0","title":["Editor's evaluation: Collaborative hunting in artificial agents with deep reinforcement learning"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-3711-8235","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Malcolm A","family":"MacIver","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"id":[{"id":"https:\/\/ror.org\/000e0be47","id-type":"ROR","asserted-by":"publisher"}],"name":"Northwestern University","place":["United States"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.7554\/elife.85694.sa0","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,4,26]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,4,26]]}},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2024.3369048","title":["S\u00b2RAM: Optimization of SRAM With Memory Access Patterns"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-4631-7412","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Woong","family":"Choi","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Electrical Engineering, Sookmyung Women&#x2019;s University, Seoul, South Korea"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2024.3369048","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2026.3720396","title":["Beyond Static Agents: A Six-Dimensional Taxonomy and Survey of Self-Evolving LLM Agents for Healthcare"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0002-6435-1988","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Shubham","family":"Vatsal","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"CIMS, New York University","place":["New York, NY, USA"],"department":["Department of Computer Science"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0000-4078-7491","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Harsh","family":"Dubey","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"CIMS, New York University","place":["New York, NY, USA"],"department":["Department of Computer Science"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0009-7677-8605","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Ahsaas","family":"Bajaj","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"University of Massachusetts Amherst","place":["Amherst, MA, USA"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2026.3720396","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2024.3356864","title":["CollabMOT Stereo Camera Collaborative Multi Object Tracking"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-7159-0771","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Phong Phu","family":"Ninh","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Electronic Engineering, Chungbuk National University, Cheongju-si, Republic of Korea"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-2602-2075","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Hyungwon","family":"Kim","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Electronic Engineering, Chungbuk National University, Cheongju-si, Republic of Korea"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2024.3356864","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.3390\/jcp4040038","title":["Reversing File Access Control Using Disk Forensics on Low-Level Flash Memory"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0007-8978-2684","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Caleb","family":"Rother","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Computer Science, Michigan Technological University, Houghton, MI 49931, USA"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-9372-9607","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Bo","family":"Chen","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Computer Science, Michigan Technological University, Houghton, MI 49931, USA"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.3390\/jcp4040038","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2024,10,1]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024,10,1]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>In the history of access control, nearly every system designed has relied on the operating system (OS) to enforce the access control protocols. However, if the OS (and specifically root access) is compromised, there are few if any solutions that can get users back into their system efficiently. In this work, we have proposed a novel approach that allows secure and efficient rollback of file access control after an adversary compromises the OS and corrupts the access control metadata. Our key observation is that the underlying flash memory typically performs out-of-place updates. Taking advantage of this unique feature, we can extract the \u201cstale data\u201d specific for OS access control, by performing low-level disk forensics over the raw flash memory. This allows efficiently rolling back the OS access control to a state pre-dating the compromise. To justify the feasibility of the proposed approach, we have implemented it in a computing device using file system EXT2\/EXT3 and open-sourced flash memory firmware OpenNFM. We also evaluated the potential impact of our design on the original system. Experimental results indicate that the performance of the affected drive is not significantly impacted.<\/jats:p>","container-title":["Journal of Cybersecurity and Privacy"]},{"DOI":"10.20944\/preprints202604.1148.v1","title":["Functional Stability and Adaptive Control in LLM-Based Computer Use Agents via Graph-Structured Persistent Memory"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0009-5822-9063","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Danylo","family":"Vorvul","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Andrii","family":"Musienko","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Iryna","family":"Galchenko","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Mykola","family":"Myroniuk","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Andrii","family":"Sobchuk","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.20944\/preprints202604.1148.v1","issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,16]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Large language model (LLM)-driven computer use agents (CUAs) automate graphical user interface (GUI) tasks but often re-solve previously encountered subtasks, increasing token use, latency, and instability. We address this limitation with a directed graph-based persistent memory in which nodes represent observable GUI states and edges encode executable action sequences. We formalize the memory-augmented agent as S=\u2329A,\u03a3,G,\u03b4,\u03c0,\u03a6\u232a, define stability conditions by analogy with functional stability theory, and derive token-cost efficiency bounds. In control-theoretic terms, the Manager\u2013Worker architecture becomes a closed-loop system where memory provides experience-based feedback, and selecting between memory retrieval and fresh LLM planning is treated as adaptive control. Experiments on OSWorld show that the proposed agent cuts both LLM token consumption and execution time by about 50% versus a memoryless baseline while preserving comparable success rates (\u224836.9% on 15-step and \u224846.9% on 50-step tasks). Structured graph memory therefore improves robustness under perturbation and supports convergent efficiency gains over time.<\/jats:p>"},{"DOI":"10.3986\/9789610507970","title":["A Memory Without Evidence"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.3986\/9789610507970","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2023,12,14]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,12,14]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>A Memory Without Evidence is a collaborative publication featuring histories and narratives of people on the move and refugees who have traversed the Balkan refugee route and managed to reach the European Union. Created through a series of workshops and dialogues with displaced communities, the collaborative publication presents the stories of those who have traded their imprisonment behind the razor wire, land mines, and systemic violence that was enforced upon them on the Balkan refugee route for being held captive by the EU asylum system. For many involved in the creation of the publication, the struggle for their existence, recognition, and freedom does not end once they reach their desired safe haven but remains a distant prospect. The writings are divided into three segments (In Prisons and Camps; Born in a Line of Displaced; 4517 Kilometres Later), each offering a critical, poetic, and in-depth reflection on different questions related to displacement and exile. The collaborative project was initiated by the photographer and artist Jos\u030ct Franko, who has coedited the publication with Zied Abdellaoui.\n\nCo-published with Moderna galerija.<\/jats:p>"},{"DOI":"10.1016\/b978-0-443-15754-7.00045-6","title":["Collaborative memory: A selective review"],"author":[{"given":"Suparna","family":"Rajaram","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Garrett D.","family":"Greeley","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Tori","family":"Pe\u00f1a","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1016\/b978-0-443-15754-7.00045-6","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"container-title":["Learning and Memory: A Comprehensive Reference"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2023.3252559","title":["Collaborative Coded Distributed Computing Scheme: A Two-Phase Cooperative Game Approach"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-1967-151X","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Sungwook","family":"Kim","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Computer Science, Sogang University, Mapo-gu, Seoul, South Korea"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2023.3252559","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.55277\/researchhub.cjra9dkr.1","title":["[Access] Long Memory Time Series Analysis"],"author":[{"given":"muna","family":"aqillunea","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.55277\/researchhub.cjra9dkr.1","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,23]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,23]]}},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2023.3303322","title":["Rating Proportion-Aware Binomial Matrix Factorization for Collaborative Filtering"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-9132-8778","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Iwao","family":"Tanuma","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Statistical Science School of Multidisciplinary Sciences, The Graduate University for Advanced Studies, Tokyo, Japan"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-3201-6106","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Tomoko","family":"Matsui","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Statistical Modeling, The Institute of Statistical Mathematics, Tokyo, Japan"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2023.3303322","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2025.3613301","title":["Multi-View Collaborative Fusion and Contrastive Learning for Recommendation"],"author":[{"given":"Shuqin","family":"Zhang","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Computer Science, Zhongyuan University of Technology, Zhengzhou, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0005-7292-8443","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Hui","family":"Zhao","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Computer Science, Zhongyuan University of Technology, Zhengzhou, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2025.3613301","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2025.3646282","title":["PreEduAI: A Multi-Agent Collaborative Framework for Automated Preschool Curriculum Development"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0002-3580-6584","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Yu","family":"Mi","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Huaibei Institute of Technology, Huaibei, Anhui, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2025.3646282","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2024.3380478","title":["Memory Integrity Techniques for Memory-Unsafe Languages: A Survey"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-2483-1648","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Vahid Eftekhari","family":"Moghadam","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Control and Computer Engineering, Politecnico di Torino, Turin, Italy"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-0225-6731","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Gabriele","family":"Serra","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"TeCIP Institute, Scuola Superiore Sant'Anna, Pisa, Italy"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0007-3537-8782","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Federico","family":"Aromolo","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"TeCIP Institute, Scuola Superiore Sant'Anna, Pisa, Italy"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-4959-4017","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Giorgio","family":"Buttazzo","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"TeCIP Institute, Scuola Superiore Sant'Anna, Pisa, Italy"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-2400-8245","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Paolo","family":"Prinetto","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Control and Computer Engineering, Politecnico di Torino, Turin, Italy"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2024.3380478","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/trustcom60117.2023.00187","title":["Access Control based on CRDTs for Collaborative Distributed Applications"],"author":[{"given":"Pierre-Antoine","family":"Rault","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Universit&#x00E9; de Lorraine,CNRS, Inria LORIA,Nancy,France,F-54000"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Claudia-Lavinia","family":"Ignat","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Universit&#x00E9; de Lorraine,CNRS, Inria LORIA,Nancy,France,F-54000"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Olivier","family":"Perrin","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Universit&#x00E9; de Lorraine,CNRS, Inria LORIA,Nancy,France,F-54000"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/trustcom60117.2023.00187","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,11,1]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,11,1]]},"container-title":["2023 IEEE 22nd International Conference on Trust, Security and Privacy in Computing and Communications (TrustCom)"]},{"DOI":"10.1007\/s40860-023-00212-w","title":["Blockchain-based collaborative business process data sharing and access control"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-1753-9857","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Xiaoxiao","family":"Sun","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Yijie","family":"Wei","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Hujun","family":"Shen","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1007\/s40860-023-00212-w","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024,3]]},"published-online":{"date-parts":[[2023,11,2]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,11,2]]},"container-title":["Journal of Reliable Intelligent Environments"]},{"DOI":"10.1093\/oxfordhb\/9780190917982.013.75","title":["Collaborative Remembering and Collective Memory"],"author":[{"given":"Suparna","family":"Rajaram","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Psychology, Stony Brook University"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1093\/oxfordhb\/9780190917982.013.75","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2024,7,18]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024,7,18]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n               <jats:p>A trip down the memory lane is often a social experience. To understand how recalling the past with others shapes one\u2019s memory, it is important to appreciate the reciprocal influences between the collective and the individual. This chapter focuses on cognitive research that examines individual and collective memories that develop in a social context. The studies reviewed in the chapter are typically experimental in nature, although some studies involved other research techniques such as surveys. The theoretical explanations reviewed identify cognitive mechanisms that operate when people engage in collaborative remembering. A confluence of these cognitive mechanisms not only influences the group memory product but also produces post-collaborative changes in what people remember and how they organize these memories. The chapter also discusses research on collaborative remembering across the life span, collaborative memory for emotional information, and the social transmission of false memories. Although collaborative memory studies have used mainly small groups, the chapter also includes recent research that uses larger groups and social networks to understand social transmission of memory. Finally, the chapter focuses on the nature of collective memory. Although collective memory has been a topic of long-held interest in sociology, anthropology, and history, recent research has brought to light psychological perspectives. In the context of studying the cognitive bases of social remembering, the chapter discusses experimental studies that are particularly relevant for understanding the relationship between collaborative remembering and collective memory.<\/jats:p>","container-title":["The Oxford Handbook of Human Memory, Two Volume Pack"]},{"DOI"